{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Hanging out with Friends"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Things I Used to Do"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le01ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Used to and Would"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> and <span class=\"strong\">used</span> to have  similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "However, there is an important difference between <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> does not require this. Read the following examples: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We would play baseball every afternoon <span class=\"underline\">when we were children</span> .<br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We used to play baseball every afternoon.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "He used to take weekly night classes and received his diploma in his twenties."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He would go to every casting call he could until someone noticed him."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the question form of used to, be careful to drop the 'd'. For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Did you <span class=\"strong\">use to</span> play baseball every afternoon?</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": " His father kicked him out at 15 and he would often sleep on people's couches!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It says here that his family used to live close to the poverty line."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Phrasal verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Phrasal verbs consist of a verb and one or more prepositions. They are often used, especially in informal spoken English. The meaning of phrasal verbs is often completely different from the meaning of the verb alone.<br/>Phrasal verbs can either be separable or inseparable."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Separable phrasal verbs consist of two parts. They always require an object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The object of a phrasal verb can go either between the verb and the preposition or after the preposition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Examples</span>:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I handed in my homework.<br/> I handed my homework in.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the object of the sentence is a pronoun, it must go between the two parts of the phrasal verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I handed it in.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some phrasal verbs are inseparable, so the verb must be directly followed by its preposition or adverb. Otherwise, the meaning of the phrasal verb will be incorrect.<br/>Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Examples</span>: <ul><li>get up = get out of bed<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I get up at seven o'clock every morning.</span></li> </ul><ul><li>take off = leave the ground <br/>         <span class=\"italic\">The plane took off on time.</span></li></ul>  <ul><li>look out = beware! be careful!<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Look out! That car is going to hit you!</span></li></ul> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Yeah, I often see him on my online feed, spending time with friends, eating out and the occasional selfie at the gym."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to say the least "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to suggest there is a lot more to a subject"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm shocked, to say the least."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you are talking about someone's past."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "charmed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very lucky"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I assumed that he had a charmed life.."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "upbringing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " how a person is raised"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He had a hard upbringing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "poverty line"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the level of income that makes it possible for a person to pay for basic food, clothing, and shelter "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It says here that his family used to live close to the poverty line."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "modelling agency"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a business that employs people to wear clothing and accessories"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I heard that he was spotted by a modelling agency in his late teens."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "casting call"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an acting audition"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He would go to every casting call he could until someone noticed him."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "online feed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "regular online updates about people and events"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I often see him on my online feed."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob08aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "selfie"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a picture that someone takes of themselves"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I take the occasional selfie at the gym."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob08aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Interview a partner or family member about their friends lifestyle."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out the names of their closest friends and the social activities they enjoy. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask about past habits. What did they used to do that they do not do anymore."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Note down any phrasal verbs they use in the conversation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a short paragraph about the person based on the interview."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Then, read the paragraph aloud to the person."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What is their response?"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I interview a person about their friends and lifestyle."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask about past habits."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a short paragraph based on notes from an interview."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write about friendships and social activiti